# PASS Cline Rules

> Non-authoritative compatibility file. PASS is being implemented with OpenCode. OpenCode should use `AGENTS.md` and the source-of-truth documents as authoritative and ignore this file for product/architecture decisions.

- Read source-of-truth docs before making architectural/product changes.
- Implement the defined product; do not invent product scope.
- First build includes web app + backend + DB + X + Ethos + Hyperliquid + Chrome extension + deployment.
- PASS is non-custodial. Never store user master private keys or seed phrases.
- Prefer client-controlled Hyperliquid agent/API wallet signing; submit signed actions to the backend only as needed.
- Account data queries use the master/subaccount address, not the agent address.
- Use official Hyperliquid APIs/SDKs and current documented signing methods.
- Validate all external data and all execution parameters.
- Pass state transitions must be auditable.
- Historical Pass records must not be silently rewritten.
- Keep Ethos reputation and trading performance separate; never synthesize a trust score.
- Extension uses Manifest V3 with minimal permissions.
- Extension enhances X discovery and hands off to the PASS web app; it does not need to manage trading keys.
- Deploy to Vercel as part of the first build.
- After deployment, iterate based on actual UX/integration findings.
- Do not claim success without tests or direct evidence.
